Don't read through null when no detail edge is found.

closestPointOnDetailEdges() starts pmin/pmax at null and sets them only for
an edge closer than FLT_MAX. When no edge qualifies (a NaN position makes
every comparison false, or the poly has no usable detail edges), it still
called dtVlerp() on them, and the server segfaulted in
dtNavMesh::closestPointOnPoly during a bots round on ns_cerbsiege_b13.
Leave closest unchanged instead.

--- a/main/source/detour/DetourNavMesh.cpp
+++ b/main/source/detour/DetourNavMesh.cpp
@@ -895,6 +895,11 @@
 			}
 		}
 
+		// No edge was found (pos is NaN, or the poly has no usable detail
+		// edges): leave closest as it is instead of reading through null.
+		if (!pmin)
+			return;
+
 		dtVlerp(closest, pmin, pmax, tmin);
 	}
 }
